\documentclass{article}
\title{Efficient Neural Rendering for Dynamic Scenes}
\author{Render Team}
\begin{document}
\maketitle
\section{Introduction}
I propose a new sampling strategy for dynamic neural radiance fields. In our framework, we model scene motion with a deformation network. One can observe that the rendering cost grows with scene complexity. I reduce this cost by caching static features between frames. Our experiments show that we achieve real-time rendering on a single GPU.
\section{Method}
The deformation network maps observation-space points into a canonical space.
\end{document}
